SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Understanding Brain Health
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nStatus: You are Confi
 rmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/186163\n\n5:00PM 
 Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\nWhat if brain health wasn’t just clinical
 —but personal\, preventative\, and deeply relevant to how we live every 
 day? In honor of Alzheimer's Awareness Month\, this candid\, forward-think
 ing conversation brings together leading physicians and patient voices to 
 explore the latest in neurovascular innovation\, life-saving interventions
 \, and the often-overlooked habits that shape cognitive well-being. Expect
  an unfiltered look at survival\, prevention\, and the science redefining 
 how we think about the brain.\n\nFeaturing Dr. Christopher Ogilvy—Direct
 or of Endovascular and Operative Neurovascular Surgery at Beth Israel Deac
 oness Medical Center and Professor at Harvard Medical School—whose pione
 ering work continues to push the boundaries of modern neurosurgery\, alon
 gside Meg Smith\, CEO of Cure Alzheimer’s Fund. Since taking the helm in
  2023\, Smith has led the organization’s continued growth and impact\, a
 dvancing a research model that has directed over $138 million toward bold 
 scientific efforts to slow\, prevent\, and ultimately reverse Alzheimer’
 s.\n\nTogether with additional expert and patient perspectives\, the panel
  offers a rare opportunity to engage with leaders at the forefront of brai
 n health and discovery.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for m
 embers only. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/186163
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
